{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze the task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01: Implement `api_call_loss_filter` through `solve(case)`.\n\nFrom the candidate artifact description:\n1. For each call, subtract loss_with_call from loss_without_call to get the gain\n2. Normalize gain by prediction_tokens (at least one)\n3. Require both parseability AND normalized gain \u003e= threshold\n4. Keep diagnostics in supplied call order\n5. Return accepted call IDs and per-call diagnostics\n\nLet me work through the logic:\n\nFor each call:\n- gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n- normalized_gain = gain / max(prediction_tokens, 1)\n- accepted = parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, tokens=5, normalized_gain = 1.56265595/5 = 0.31253119, parseable=true, threshold=0.05 → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, tokens=4, normalized_gain = 0.37796304/4 = 0.09449076, parseable=true, threshold=0.05 → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, tokens=6, normalized_gain = 0.74550131/6 = 0.12425022, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, tokens=5, normalized_gain = 0.7595393/5 = 0.1519079, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, tokens=5, normalized_gain = 0.20983801/5 = 0.04196760, parseable=true, threshold=0.05 → NOT accepted (below threshold)\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, tokens=4, normalized_gain = 0.76393214/4 = 0.19098304, parseable=true → accepted\n\nSo accepted_call_ids = [\"call0\", \"call1\", \"call2\", \"call3\", \"call5\"]\n\nNow let me code this up. The description mentions \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I need to figure out the rounding. The schema says `normalized_gain` is a `number` type, so I'll keep it as a float. The word \"rounded\" might just mean formatted to some decimal places, but since the schema just says number, I'll keep full precision.\n\nWait, \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - I'll just return the float as-is since the schema says number.\n\nLet me write the solve function:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / max(prediction_tokens, 1)\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me validate against case-002 where call4 has parseable=false:\n- call4: gain = 1.35899862 - 0.11897463 = 1.24002399, tokens=4, normalized_gain = 0.31000599, parseable=false → NOT accepted (not parseable)\n\nNow I need to format this as the strict submission envelope: a single JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a JSON string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / max(prediction_tokens, 1)\\n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_013TLsErl1tOdoThYxPigByT","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2470},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2470,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":49,"output_tokens":1302,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1048},"service_tier":"standard"}}